@title bit Generations - Soundvoyager (Japan)
@file Bit Generations Soundvoyager (J).gba
@game BVGJ
@chip SRAM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: the game formats its 32 KB SRAM at the first boot ("SND" header and defaults, the same 16 bytes in all three); progress is written only when a stage is cleared, and sound catcher's first stage soon dims its targets to nothing: past ten catches (f14941) they can only be found by ear

# Health warning, A, the Soundvoyager logo, A: "press start", START, adjust
# volume, A: the LR balance screen, R, A, UP to the mode tree's "sound
# catcher (voyage)", A: stage 1. The sound source shows as a green ring
# coming down the field; LEFT/RIGHT slide the field under the player (the
# grey dot at the bottom): RIGHT moves the ring left. The ring is steered
# over the player twice (caught at f3939 and f4977), the third one entering
# at the top ends the script. dingbat-bios, mgba and the second reference
# hash alike through most of it; the fades in and out of each screen (the
# meter's frame, the player dot) come out a shade apart.

